  "notes": "Ichidan verb ({一段動詞|いちだんどうし}).\n- Negative: {欠|か}けない\n- Polite: {欠|か}けます\n- Te-form: {欠|か}けて\n- Past: {欠|か}けた\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\nIntransitive ({自動詞|じどうし}). The transitive counterpart is {欠|か}く (to chip something, to lack something).\n\nTEIRU FORM:\n{欠|か}けている describes a state of being chipped or being in a condition where something is lacking.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {歯|は}が{欠|か}ける: a tooth gets chipped\n- {茶碗|ちゃわん}が{欠|か}ける: a bowl gets chipped\n- {月|つき}が{欠|か}ける: the moon wanes\n- {人数|にんずう}が{欠|か}ける: to be short on people\n- {欠|か}けた{部分|ぶぶん}: the chipped/missing part",
